    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-1220",
      "problem": "The graph below shows the curve $y=3^{x}+c$ . What is the value of $c?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14220062/assets/00264eb90dbaa2c50fdd626d61292c0428fd0bbbd03a6d051353598450b4ad89.png)",
      "worked_solution": "The horizontal asymptote of $y=3^x$ is $y=0.$ The vertical translation $y=3^x+c$ shifts the asymptote to $y=c.$\n\nIn the graph above, the horizontal asymptote is $y=2.$ Therefore, $c=2.$",
